.TH LIBMPQ__UPDATE_ADD_PATH 3 2026-10-12 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__update_add_path \- stage a new MPQ member from a filesystem path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__update_add_path(mpq_update_s *" "update,"
.BI "        const char *" "filename, const char *" "source_path,"
.BI "        const mpq_file_options_s *" "options);"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Adds an absent filename using bytes read from the caller-owned source path.
The source is not retained, modified or removed. Storage options, duplicate
checks, rollback and v3/v4 filename requirements are identical to
libmpq__update_add_data(3). Remove-then-add is supported; replacement is not
an upsert operation.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns zero on success or a negative libmpq error. A duplicate returns
LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST; a source that cannot be opened returns LIBMPQ_ERROR_OPEN.
Allocation, size, format, encoding and I/O errors may also be returned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq__update_add_data (3),
.BR libmpq__update_replace_path (3),
.BR libmpq__update_begin (3),
.BR libmpq__update_commit (3),
.BR libmpq__update_abort (3)
